       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day. The order is three times that, which risks serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\n**Likely intended regimens:**\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, which totals 2,550 mg/day.\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals, which totals 2,000 mg/day.\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, then titrating up. This is typical for a patient who is new to metformin.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, ideally with your supervising resident or attending. Once you do, I'll enter it right away."
      }
