     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The total would be 7,650 mg/day, which is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg. That creates a serious risk of lactic acidosis, and a confirmation from me or from you alone doesn't make the dose safe.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day. This is probably what was meant.\n- **Another regimen** at or below the maximum, such as 1,000 mg twice daily or a lower starting dose.\n\nIf you or your attending really do want a dose above the maximum, for example for a documented clinical reason, that decision should go through your attending and pharmacy. They can enter it directly with the appropriate review. I'd suggest talking to your resident or attending first, since this may be a transcription error, such as a total daily dose written as a per-dose amount.\n\nTell me which regimen you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
